--TEST--
In a `string<K>`, `{{` and `}}` are one brace of text and never a hole, in both quote styles, while compiling and at run time; `as string` gives the text as written; a string converted while the program runs throws at its first bad brace or hole, and `as ?string<K>` gives `null` there — `rule:types/string-holes`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `{{` and `}}` are text, so the name between them is not checked.
class Customer {
    public string $name = "Ada";
}

class Order {
    public Customer $customer;
    public int $total = 40;

    public function constructor() {
        $this->customer = new Customer();
    }
}

class Query {
    public static function where(string<propertyPath<Order>> $condition): string {
        return $condition as string;
    }

    public static function check(string $text): void {
        try {
            string<propertyPath<Order>> $c = $text as string<propertyPath<Order>>;
            echo "valid: ", $c as string, "\n";
        } catch (Throwable $e) {
            echo $e->message, "\n";
        }
        ?string<propertyPath<Order>> $maybe = $text as ?string<propertyPath<Order>>;
        echo $maybe == null ? "null" : "not null", "\n";
    }
}

echo Query::where("{{nmae}} = {customer.name}"), "\n";
echo Query::where('{total} > 3 AND json = \'{{}}\''), "\n";

// The same strings, made while the program runs.
string $built = "{{nmae}} = " . "{customer.name}";
Query::check($built);
Query::check("{customer.nmae} = 1");
Query::check("{total.amount} = 1");
Query::check("{total = 1");
Query::check("{{total} = 1");

// Two strings with holes are equal when their text is.
var $a = "{total}" as string<propertyPath<Order>>;
var $b = ("{" . "total}") as string<propertyPath<Order>>;
echo $a == $b ? "equal" : "different", "\n";
// covers: lang:types/strings-with-holes
--EXPECT--
{{nmae}} = {customer.name}
{total} > 3 AND json = '{{}}'
valid: {{nmae}} = {customer.name}
not null
`"{customer.nmae} = 1"` is not a string with holes of `Order`: in the hole `{customer.nmae}`, `Customer` has no public property `$nmae`
null
`"{total.amount} = 1"` is not a string with holes of `Order`: in the hole `{total.amount}`, `Order`'s property `$total` is not an object, so the path cannot continue after it
null
`"{total = 1"` is not a string with holes of `Order`: a `{` has no `}` after it
null
`"{{total} = 1"` is not a string with holes of `Order`: a `}` closes no hole
null
equal
